LinearRegression()
python
LinearRegression(
    fit_intercept=True,
    copy_X=True,
    tol=1e-6,
    n_jobs=None,
    positive=False
)
Param	Default	What it does
fit_intercept	True	Whether to calculate an intercept (bias term). Set False only if you know data passes through origin.
copy_X	True	Copies X before fitting instead of overwriting it in place.
tol	1e-6	Precision tolerance for the solver's stopping criterion.
n_jobs	None	CPU cores to use for computation (-1 = all cores). Only helps for multi-target or large sparse problems.
positive	False	If True, forces all coefficients to be non-negative.

(No alpha — plain linear regression has no regularization, so nothing to tune here — this is why GridSearchCV on LinearRegression alone is pointless.)

Ridge()
python
Ridge(
    alpha=1.0,
    fit_intercept=True,
    copy_X=True,
    max_iter=None,
    tol=1e-4,
    solver='auto',
    positive=False,
    random_state=None
)
Param	Default	What it does
alpha	1.0	L2 penalty strength. Higher = more shrinkage. This is the main one you tune.
fit_intercept	True	Same as above.
copy_X	True	Same as above.
max_iter	None	Max iterations for iterative solvers (only used by some solver choices).
tol	1e-4	Solver precision/stopping tolerance.
solver	'auto'	Algorithm: 'auto', 'svd', 'cholesky', 'lsqr', 'sparse_cg', 'sag', 'saga', 'lbfgs'. 'auto' picks automatically based on data.
positive	False	Forces non-negative coefficients (only supported by 'lbfgs' solver).
random_state	None	Seed, only relevant for 'sag'/'saga' solvers (they're stochastic).
Lasso()
python
Lasso(
    alpha=1.0,
    fit_intercept=True,
    precompute=False,
    copy_X=True,
    max_iter=1000,
    tol=1e-4,
    warm_start=False,
    positive=False,
    random_state=None,
    selection='cyclic'
)
Param	Default	What it does
alpha	1.0	L1 penalty strength. Main tuning param — can zero out coefficients entirely.
fit_intercept	True	Same as above.
precompute	False	Use a precomputed Gram matrix to speed up fitting on large datasets.
copy_X	True	Same as above.
max_iter	1000	Max iterations of the coordinate descent solver. You bumped this to 10000 because the default often isn't enough for it to converge.
tol	1e-4	Convergence tolerance.
warm_start	False	If True, reuses the previous fit's solution as a starting point (useful when refitting repeatedly with slightly different params).
positive	False	Forces non-negative coefficients.
random_state	None	Seed for the 'random' feature-selection order (only relevant if selection='random').
selection	'cyclic'	How coordinate descent picks which feature to update each step: 'cyclic' (in order) or 'random' (often converges faster).
ElasticNet()
python
ElasticNet(
    alpha=1.0,
    l1_ratio=0.5,
    fit_intercept=True,
    precompute=False,
    max_iter=1000,
    copy_X=True,
    tol=1e-4,
    warm_start=False,
    positive=False,
    random_state=None,
    selection='cyclic'
)

Same as Lasso, plus:

Param	Default	What it does
l1_ratio	0.5	Blend between L1 (Lasso) and L2 (Ridge). 0 = pure Ridge, 1 = pure Lasso. Second main tuning param alongside alpha.
Pipeline() and GridSearchCV() themselves
python
Pipeline(
    steps,
    memory=None,
    verbose=False
)
Param	What it does
steps	List of (name, transformer/estimator) tuples — the only one you've used.
memory	Cache intermediate step results to disk (avoids recomputing on repeated pipeline runs — useful with slow preprocessing).
verbose	Prints timing info for each step when fitting.
python
GridSearchCV(
    estimator,
    param_grid,
    scoring=None,
    n_jobs=None,
    refit=True,
    cv=None,
    verbose=0,
    error_score=np.nan,
    return_train_score=False
)
Param	Default	What it does
estimator	—	The pipeline/model to tune.
param_grid	—	Dict or list of dicts of hyperparameters to search.
scoring	None	Metric to optimize for (defaults to the estimator's own .score() if not set — r2 for regressors).
n_jobs	None	Parallelism.
refit	True	Automatically refits the best combo on the full training set — this is why grid.predict() works directly.
cv	None	Number of folds (or a CV splitter object). Default is 5 if left None.
verbose	0	Prints progress as it searches; higher numbers = more detail.
error_score	np.nan	What to do/report if a fit fails on some combo instead of crashing the whole search.
return_train_score	False	If True, also reports training-set scores (not just validation) in cv_results_ — useful for spotting overfitting.

For your notes, the ones worth actually memorizing (the rest you'll rarely touch) are: alpha, l1_ratio, max_iter, fit_intercept, solver (Ridge only), and on the search side cv, scoring, n_jobs, refit.

Here's the full parameter reference for the other common prediction models — the ones from your earlier blueprint, now with every parameter, not just the tuned ones.

DecisionTreeRegressor()
python
DecisionTreeRegressor(
    criterion='squared_error',
    splitter='best',
    max_depth=None,
    min_samples_split=2,
    min_samples_leaf=1,
    min_weight_fraction_leaf=0.0,
    max_features=None,
    random_state=None,
    max_leaf_nodes=None,
    min_impurity_decrease=0.0,
    ccp_alpha=0.0
)
Param	Default	What it does
criterion	'squared_error'	How split quality is measured: 'squared_error', 'friedman_mse', 'absolute_error', 'poisson'.
splitter	'best'	'best' picks the optimal split each time; 'random' picks among random splits (faster, more regularized).
max_depth	None	Max tree depth. None = grows until leaves are pure — usually overfits, so this is your #1 tuning knob.
min_samples_split	2	Min samples a node needs before it's allowed to split further.
min_samples_leaf	1	Min samples required in a leaf node. Raising this smooths the model out.
min_weight_fraction_leaf	0.0	Same idea as above but as a fraction of total sample weight.
max_features	None	How many features to consider per split. None = all features.
random_state	None	Seed for reproducibility (splitter has some randomness).
max_leaf_nodes	None	Caps total number of leaf nodes.
min_impurity_decrease	0.0	A split only happens if it reduces impurity by at least this much.
ccp_alpha	0.0	Cost-complexity pruning strength — higher values prune more branches after the tree is built.
