)

All the DecisionTreeRegressor params apply per-tree, plus:

Param	Default	What it does
n_estimators	100	Number of trees in the forest. More = generally better but slower, diminishing returns past a point.
bootstrap	True	Whether each tree trains on a random resampled subset of rows (bagging).
oob_score	False	If True and bootstrap=True, uses leftover "out-of-bag" samples to estimate performance without a separate validation set.
n_jobs	None	Parallelize tree-building across cores.
verbose	0	Print progress while fitting.
warm_start	False	Add more trees to an existing fitted forest instead of starting over.
max_samples	None	If bootstrap=True, how many samples each tree draws (default = full dataset size, with replacement).
GradientBoostingRegressor()
python
GradientBoostingRegressor(
    loss='squared_error',
    learning_rate=0.1,
    n_estimators=100,
    subsample=1.0,
    criterion='friedman_mse',
    min_samples_split=2,
    min_samples_leaf=1,
    min_weight_fraction_leaf=0.0,
    max_depth=3,
    min_impurity_decrease=0.0,
    random_state=None,
