    validation_fraction=0.1,
    n_iter_no_change=None,
    tol=1e-4,
    ccp_alpha=0.0
)
Param	Default	What it does
loss	'squared_error'	Loss function: 'squared_error', 'absolute_error', 'huber', 'quantile'.
learning_rate	0.1	Shrinks each tree's contribution. Lower = needs more trees but often generalizes better. Trade-off with n_estimators.
n_estimators	100	Number of boosting stages (sequential trees).
subsample	1.0	Fraction of rows used per tree (< 1.0 adds randomness, like bagging).
max_depth	3	Depth per tree — kept shallow by default since boosting builds many weak trees.
validation_fraction	0.1	Portion of training data held out for early stopping (only used if n_iter_no_change is set).
n_iter_no_change	None	Stops boosting early if validation score doesn't improve for this many rounds.
tol	1e-4	Tolerance for early stopping.
alpha	0.9	Only used with loss='huber' or 'quantile' — sets the quantile.
ccp_alpha	0.0	Same pruning idea as decision tree.
